														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852690">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight</strong> Yes<br />
<strong>Page Type</strong> SCP Article<br />
<strong>Genre</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong><br />
This anomaly does not have an appearance but from signs of consuming its designated slot and neighboring slots through usages of biting and tearing texts and images apart.</p>
<p>The document/data concerning this entity must be periodically moved to a different slot when signs of consumption and degradation start to show in the file.</p>
<p>If the entity does not get relocated, then it will start devouring neighboring SCPs, &quot;deleting&quot; them from the database&quot; and literally, making them become non-existent along with related sites, staff, and personnel.</p>
<p>This SCP is not a virus in the database as it has the ability to erase things it consumes from existence in the SCP universe. The location where the deleted site/anomalies used to be will be replaced with a black void, signifying a hole in reality itself. Because of the reality bending effects it left, it is designated an infohazard/cognitohazard Keter anomaly. Observing the tear in reality caused the observers to become &quot;aware&quot; of its fictional status, and aware of entities from higher dimensions (the authors) who have the power to influence and shape their universe.</p>
<p>This ever-hunger entity can cause an end-of-reality scenario if left unchecked, so the O5 planned to cause global extinction as being terminated is a better fate than to be &quot;deleted&quot;, or so they belived.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong><br />
This will be presented by normal means of containing (constant relocation of the anomaly) while hiding its true nature (that it cannot be permanently contained and that it caused things to become non-existent). And fake description/containment procedures to keep people from panicking and becoming aware of their fictional world. This implies that in the future, it may devours its designated slot faster than the foundation could even react.</p>
<p>Experimental logs involving D-Class getting send into the void, MTF getting erased from the database as they explore the deleted site and list of &quot;known&quot; deleted anomalies that the foundation somehow still have the record.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber</strong><br />
The document ending will be left vague after all the interviews, logs, failed neutralization attempt and how the GOC tried to use this anomaly without knowing the after-effect. This will left the reader to imagine if they all died (from O5 explosion), wiped out from the conflict between GOC and the foundation, or something else entirely.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes</strong><br />
None</p>

