			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852648">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights:** Yes.</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre: Horror/Comedy</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A mysterious software appears along with a mysterious PC out of nowhere and seems to grant mindless beings knowledge to act as sapient beings. However, they can't recall their past nor origin and seem to have only a small piece of their memories.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This software was discovered when one of the Foundation personnel noticed strange sounds from one of the enhanced containment chambers that're containing non-sapient SCPs. They discovered that it is talking and chatting on a PC that shows up out of nowhere.</p>
<p>This SCP originally is a PC that appears to have an unknown chatroom with unidentified programmers. This chatroom's software is named &quot;The Humanoids,&quot; seemingly designed for both sapient and non-sapient anomalies to interact with each other through the technology screens. Any non-sapient/mindless humanoid entities/beings who come in contact with the screen will eventually be granted the knowledge to act as beings that aren't mindless. Of course, they may also embody human nature and act like regular humans, and some act very smart.</p>
<p>However, despite being granted sapient knowledge, the humanoid entities cannot remember their origins, and some seem only to recall a small piece of their memories.</p>
<p>Attempted to delete the software or destroy the PC is proven to be impossible, for it is shown to be constructed out of mysterious unidentified materials and seemingly has a powerful firewall to prevent hackers from infiltrating into it. However, the Foundation didn't try their best efforts in an attempt to erase the software nor wreck the PC, for it is because, with the help of &quot;The Humanoids&quot; chatroom, the hostile non-sapient SCPs appear to have good behaviors rather than being hostile, evil, and aggressive. However, the chatroom doesn't actually change the behaviors of sapient SCPs as they still have their original personalities.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> For those of you who have watched or read <em>&quot;Durarara&quot;</em> then this SCP was inspired by the <em>&quot;Dollar's&quot;</em> chatroom of the <em>&quot;Durarara&quot;</em> series.
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Draft is work in progress.</p>

							</div>

								
					
