<p>With all due respect: no.</p>
<p>This is just&#8230;.shock horror in the most uninteresting way, with absolutely no respect for the topics you're writing about. Like, the absolute cruelty towards women present here is uncomfortable in a way that I don't really vibe with, and which I think you're aware of.</p>
<p>But there's also little things like you mentioning &quot;It’s similar to the Buddhist “blood bowl sutra.”&quot; followed by &quot;Starts with local Shinto priest interview, warning of it and an entity underneath.&quot; which to me heavily implies you aren't aware that Buddhism and Shintoism aren't the same thing. This feels like it's just using a generic mishmash of east asian tropes as a cover to tell a story that's fundamentally revelling in the horror of women being murdered and there's no parts of this that I like or particularly wish to see being developed further.</p>

