<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Yeah, idk. I think really my question here is why the Foundation would write a SCP article about this: it's something they made and are utilising, and it's not even necessarily that anomalous; so it seems like all an in-universe article about this would do would be create a way by which people could realise this is the case when they shouldn't?</p>
<p>This kinda feels like it'd work best as a tale: I can totally see this really cool intrigue piece where like, someone working at a UIU/Foundation site realises that something weird is going on and like, gradually starts piecing stuff together before realising that hey, they aren't actually in the Foundation and are actually a member of the UIU and then they have to try and do something to put an end to this without being discovered and amnesticised.</p>
<p>My problem with this as a SCP is that effectively the article is positioned in a way where nothing interesting can happen: we can't really see the cool story of how the Foundation pulled this off without the UIU realising; and we can't really see a story of someone figuring out this has happened and like trying to stop it; and so there's not really a lot of room for you to do anything interesting with it? I also don't really think that just setting up what happened here is interesting enough because it doesn't really have&#8230;a sense of there being consequences cos this happened? Like, a short article where you piece together this happened could almost work as long as there's a bit where it makes you realise why what happened is shocking and I'm not sure this has that?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

